<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brougham</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Brocavum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brougham is a village near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penrith">Penrith</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumbria">Cumbria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, at the crossing of the River Eamont. It was the site of the Roman fort of Brocavum, whose cemetery and inscriptions, including a milestone naming the civitas of the Carvetii, have been found nearby. The medieval Brougham Castle stands on part of the fort.</p></div>
